{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SkewBranchingSum","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SkewBranchingSum","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SkewSYTBranchingBijection","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.YoungLatticeCornerCount"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.factorial_mul_skewPair_of_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.factorial_mul_skewPair_of_le","kind":"theorem","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SkewBranchingSum.lean#L231-L236","doc":"The same, indexed by the target size rather than by the increment. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.factorial_mul_skewPair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.factorial_mul_skewPair","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SkewBranchingSum.lean#L207-L229","doc":"**The classical branching sum, divisor-free.**\n\n|μ|! · ∑_{λ of size |μ|+d}  f^λ · f^{λ/μ}  =  (|μ|+d)! · f^μ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.skewPair_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.skewPair_succ","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SkewBranchingSum.lean#L158-L205","doc":"**The step.**  For `k ≥ |μ|`, `G(μ, k+1) = (k+1)·G(μ, k)`.\n\nExpand `f^{λ/μ}` by `fDimSkew_branching_corners`, reindex the `(λ, corner)` pairs as\n`(ν, addable cell)` pairs by `rankExchange` (which sends `(λ, c)` to `(λ ∖ c, c)`), and collapse\nthe resulting inner sum with `upSum_eq`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.skewPair_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.skewPair_card","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SkewBranchingSum.lean#L140-L155","doc":"**The base case.**  At `k = |μ|` the only diagram containing `μ` is `μ` itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.skewPair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.skewPair","kind":"def","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SkewBranchingSum.lean#L136-L138","doc":"`G(μ, k) = ∑_{λ of size k} f^λ · f^{λ/μ}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.fDimSkew_branching_corners","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.fDimSkew_branching_corners","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SkewBranchingSum.lean#L92-L132","doc":"**Skew branching over ALL corners.**  The corners lying inside `inner` contribute `0`, so\nthe restricted sum of `fDimSkew_branching` may be widened to the full corner subtype — which is\nthe index `rankExchange` speaks about. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.fDimSkew_eraseCorner_eq_zero_of_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.fDimSkew_eraseCorner_eq_zero_of_mem","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SkewBranchingSum.lean#L85-L90","doc":"A corner inside `inner` contributes nothing: deleting it breaks the containment. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.eraseCorner_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.eraseCorner_le","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SkewBranchingSum.lean#L78-L83","doc":"Deleting a corner shrinks the diagram. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.fDimSkew_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.fDimSkew_self","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SkewBranchingSum.lean#L67-L76","doc":"**`f^{μ/μ} = 1`.**  The skew region is empty, so `zeros` forces every entry and the filling\nabove is the only one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.skewSelfTableau","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.skewSelfTableau","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SkewBranchingSum.lean#L55-L65","doc":"The empty filling of the empty skew shape `μ/μ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}